Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::a_transfer_command_addresses_only_logical_blocks_the_namespace_has`.

The defect: `Namespace::transfer_command` computes the starting logical block as if every format
had 512-byte logical blocks, multiplying the block number by `unit_bytes / 512` instead of by the
stored `blocks_per_transfer`. On a namespace formatted with 4096-byte logical blocks the command
then names a logical block eight times too far along, while the byte bound still passes.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(starting_logical_block + blocks <= namespace_blocks)`.

diff --git a/src/namespace.rs b/src/namespace.rs
--- a/src/namespace.rs
+++ b/src/namespace.rs
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
         if !self.holds_whole_block(block) {
             return None;
         }
-        let starting_logical_block = block.checked_mul(u64::from(self.blocks_per_transfer))?;
+        let starting_logical_block = block.checked_mul(self.unit_bytes / 512)?;
         let pages =
             physical_region_page_pair(data_physical_address, self.unit_bytes, page_size_bytes)?;
         let blocks = self.blocks_per_transfer;
